    "status": "needs_review",
    "verified_answer": "2010.62 cm^3",
    "issue": "8 cm is marked from the cross-section center to the rim, so it is the radius. Volume for a half-cylinder of radius 8 cm and length 20 cm is 0.5*pi*8^2*20=2010.62 cm^3, conflicting with raw GT 502.65, which requires radius 4 cm.",
